{"tool_name":"gs-preprocess","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"gs-preprocess","home":"http://github.com/umasstr/GS-Preprocess","summary":"Containerized GUIDE-seq Data Analysis Tools with Diverse Sequencer Compatibility.\n\nGS-Preprocess is a one-line, 6-argument pipeline that generates input data for the GUIDEseq Bioconductor package (https://doi.org/doi:10.18129/B9.bioc.GUIDEseq) from raw Illumina sequencer output. For off-target profiling, Bioconductor GUIDEseq only requires a 2-line guideRNA fasta, demultiplexed BAM files of \"plus\"- and \"minus\"-strands, and Unique Molecular Index (UMI) references for each read.\n\nExpected Runtime and Resource Usage.\n\nSample Bioconductor GUIDEseq Input.","addition_date":"2021-01-18T07:03:20Z","last_update_date":"2021-01-25T11:32:46Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:gs-preprocess","credit":[{"email":"Julie.Zhu@umassmed.edu","name":"Lihua Julie Zhu","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"Tomas.Rodriguez@umassmed.edu","name":"Tom\u00e1s C. Rodr\u00edguez","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Demultiplexing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3933"},{"term":"Read pre-processing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3219"},{"term":"Sequence trimming","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3192"}]}],"name":"GS-Preprocess","owner":"Niclaskn","publication":[{"doi":"10.1101/2020.01.26.914861"}],"topic":[{"term":"Probes and primers","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0632"},{"term":"Sequencing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3168"},{"term":"Workflows","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0769"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"GS-Preprocess","home":"https://bio.tools/gs-preprocess","summary":"Containerized GUIDE-seq Data Analysis Tools with Diverse Sequencer Compatibility.\n\nGS-Preprocess is a one-line, 6-argument pipeline that generates input data for the GUIDEseq Bioconductor pac